			"notes": "Promenade has been updated to run on **Minecraft 26.3**!\n\nAnd for the first time ever, it supports the **NeoForge** mod loader!\n\n## NeoForge Support\nPromenade now supports NeoForge! This was of the most requested feature, so I'm very stoked to see how will people will enjoy it in new ways.\n\n- Every future version will support both Fabric and NeoForge loaders\n- Fabric and NeoForge versions are uploaded side by side, and their changelog is the same\n  - Please make sure you are downloading the correct version\n- The NeoForge part is mostly a 1-to-1 port of the Fabric one.\n  - This means gameplay should be exactly the same no matter what loader you are using.\n  - Only exceptions are: accessibility of configuration screens (see below), biome additions (new mobs and such) and internal registration\n\n## Additions\n- Added an in-game configuration screen for managing the config file.\n  - It is accessible through the Mod Menu mod for Fabric users, and the built-in mods menu for NeoForge users.\n\n## Changes\n- Worldgen modifications powered by Biolith are now added through datapacks.\n  - This means biome distribution is no longer managed through the config file, but can still be configured using datapacks.\n  - Please refer to the wiki for updated information on ways to configure Promenade."
		},
